// The inventory screen open on the Rocket tab over the seeded map at the start, the game playing
// (the screen hides while paused). The stock: iron plates (30), copper plates (10), the factory
// (1) and wire (6), then eleven empty sockets; nothing is selected. The construct section: the
// Rocket tab active (amber, underlined), the Buildings tab dark; the four rocket parts with their
// keys F, G, H and J at their top left, the engine, the fuel storage and the cargo bay orderable,
// the life support dim (with its electronics it takes 13 copper plates, 10 are held). The info
// panel below the screen shows the factory of its stock slot, as if hovered: its icon and name,
// "Ready to place - 75 W" in amber, "Speeds up crafting." and no needs. The Inventory (E) button
// at the bottom center.
include apps/oreelse/test/visual/setup/seed
include apps/oreelse/etc/oreelse

using box.camera
using box.surface
using oreelse

// The capture is 640x360: the HUD lays out for a 1280x720 window and its camera shows it at
// half size, so the capture holds the whole screen as a 1280x720 window shows it
window {
  Surface: {width: 1280, height: 720}
}

hud {
  ui {
    camera {
      Camera: {ortho: true, ortho_scale: 0.5}
    }
  }
}

// The pointer is over no element: OreItemInfo names the stock slot of the factory as the UI
// would, and OreItemInfoUpdate derives the item of the info panel
$ {
  (OreGameState, Playing)
  OreInventory: {
    slots: [
      {item: items.IronPlate, amount: 30},
      {item: items.CopperPlate, amount: 10},
      {item: Factory, amount: 1},
      {item: items.Wire, amount: 6}
    ]
  }
  OreInventoryScreen: {open: true, tab: 1}
  OreItemInfo: {slot: 2, button: 0, item: 0, place: false}
}
